  "limits": [
    "Canonical app entry declarations are conditional type assumptions, not pointer validity or current numeric targets. Cross-domain/unknown writes conservatively block those declarations; explicit local stores remain usable.",
    "Runtime homogeneous table role tags are not full arbitrary serialized-value identities. Null/serialization phases and opaque saved incoming bases remain separate obligations, not new global reader seeds.",
    "The source-backed header-directory loop still reproduces a missing bounded selection contract: straight-line fixture passes, two-entry DBF loop fails. Existing source-table reconciliation rejects widened unknown selectors; no value cap or evidence guard is relaxed. Next experiment is shared source-cursor induction and homogeneous domain proof, including invalid/one-past/mixed-entry negatives.",
    "No new normal-input flight, gameplay, DMA or timing observation. Original data ownership and byte layout are independently checked; more typed facts alone are not all-path proof."
  ],
